  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange the World-Celebration of the 16 Days of Activism against GBV in Cairo 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x201c;Orange the World&#x201d; campaign, held during the 16 Days of Activism, is a global initiative calling for an end to gender-based violence. Led by the UN, it raises awareness of the human rights dimensions of violence against women and girls, mobilising governments, civil society, the media, and communities to advocate for prevention, survivor-centred responses, and stronger protection systems. The campaign also promotes political commitment and resources to address root inequalities and support those in crisis settings.

In 2025, a five-day community carnival will take place from 18&#x2013;22 December, featuring panels, workshops, theatre, film screenings, and art exhibitions focused on GBV and survivor journeys. The embassy will spotlight technology-facilitated violence, drawing on lessons from project 24-0000729</narrative>
  </description>
